./data/docling_include_no_vlm_2026-07-09/chunks/full_2026_07_06_rec_001358.jsonl:118:{"candidate_id": "full_2026-07-06__rec_001358", "chunk_index": 118, "text": "Supplementary Figure 19: Dot plots showing cell-state specificity of the top 30 attentionranked  genes  from  (a)  native  scGPT,  (b)  finetuned  scGPT,  and  (c)  scPEFT  comparing Memory CD8+ T cells and Naïve CD8+ T cells in the COVID-19 dataset. Dot size represents the fraction of cells in each state, while color indicates log fold change. The target cell state is highlighted, with function-associated genes investigated in this study outlined by boxes.\nSupplementary Figure 20: Dot plots showing cell-state specificity of the top 30 attentionranked  genes  from  (a)  native  scGPT,  (b)  finetuned  scGPT,  and  (c)  scPEFT  comparing Effector Memory CD8+ T cells and memory CD8+ T cells in the COVID-19 dataset. Dot size represents the fraction of cells in each state, while color indicates log fold change. The target cell state is highlighted, with function-associated genes investigated in this study outlined by boxes.", "contextualized_text": "Harnessing the power of single-cell large language models with parameter-efficient fine-tuning using scPEFT\nSupplementary Figures\nSupplementary Figure 19: Dot plots showing cell-state specificity of the top 30 attentionranked  genes  from  (a)  native  scGPT,  (b)  finetuned  scGPT,  and  (c)  scPEFT  comparing Memory CD8+ T cells and Naïve CD8+ T cells in the COVID-19 dataset. Dot size represents the fraction of cells in each state, while color indicates log fold change. The target cell state is highlighted, with function-associated genes investigated in this study outlined by boxes.\nSupplementary Figure 20: Dot plots showing cell-state specificity of the top 30 attentionranked  genes  from  (a)  native  scGPT,  (b)  finetuned  scGPT,  and  (c)  scPEFT  comparing Effector Memory CD8+ T cells and memory CD8+ T cells in the COVID-19 dataset. Dot size represents t