./data/docling_include_no_vlm_2026-07-09/chunks/full_2026_07_06_rec_001358.jsonl:122:{"candidate_id": "full_2026-07-06__rec_001358", "chunk_index": 122, "text": "Supplementary Figure 24: Performance of adapter combinations in scPEFT for cell type identification on the NSCLC dataset using scGPT as the backbone. a-f, Violin plots showing balanced accuracy from 5-fold cross-validation for all dual-adapter combinations, alongside their respective  individual  adapters  as  baselines.  Annotated  values  indicate  performance  gains  or losses  relative  to  the  baselines.  Heatmaps  below  each  plot  illustrate  the  relative  number  of learnable parameters and GPU memory usage for each configuration. The darker cells in these heatmaps represent higher resource consumption. Statistical significance between the combined and individual adapters was assessed using a paired two-sided Student's t-test across the fivefold validation results (n=5 independent validation tests). On each box, the central mark indicates the median, and the bottom and top edges of the box indicate the 25th and 75th percentiles. The whiskers extend to the most extreme data points without outliers, and the outliers are plotted individually  as  circles. g-j, Benchmark  results  comparing  triple-adapter  combinations", "contextualized_text": "Harnessing the power of single-cell large language models with parameter-efficient fine-tuning using scPEFT\nSupplementary Figures\nSupplementary Figure 24: Performance of adapter combinations in scPEFT for cell type identification on the NSCLC dataset using scGPT as the backbone. a-f, Violin plots showing balanced accuracy from 5-fold cross-validation for all dual-adapter combinations, alongside their respective  individual  adapters  as  baselines.  Annotated  values  indicate  performance  gains  or losses  relative  to  the  baselines.  Heatmaps  below  each  plot  illustrate  the  relative  number  of learnable parameters and GPU memory usage for each configuration. The darker cells in these heatmaps represent higher resource consumption. Statistical significance between the combined and individual adapters was assessed using a paired two-sided Student's t-test across the fivefold validation results (n=5 independent validation tests). On each box, the central mark indicates the median, and the bottom and top edges of the box indicate the 25th and 75th percentiles. The whiskers extend to the most extreme data points without outliers, and the outliers are plotted individually  as  circles. g-j, Benchmark  results  comparing  triple-adapter  combinations", "headings": ["Harnessing the power of single-cell large language models with parameter-efficient fine-tuning using scPEFT", "Supplementary Figures"], "pages": [56], "meta": {"schema_name": "docling_core.transforms.chunker.DocMeta", "version": "1.0.0", "doc_items": [{"self_ref": "#/texts/238", "parent": {"cref": "#/body"}, "children": [], "content_layer": "body", "meta": null, "label": "text", "prov": [{"page_no": 56, "bbox": {"l": 72.0, "t": 717.5846399999999, "r": 543.1211999999998, "b": 518.7083053259669, "coord_origin": "BOTTOMLEFT"}, "charspan": [0, 1260]}]}], "headings": ["Harnessing the power of single-cell large language models with parameter-efficient fine-tuning using scPEFT", "Supplementary Figures"], "captions": null, "origin": {"mimetype": "application/pdf", "binary_hash": 3578786038470275027, "filename": "full_text_02_landing_pdf_link.pdf", "uri": null}}}
