./data/docling_include_no_vlm_2026-07-09/markdown/full_2026_07_06_rec_001358.md:439:Supplementary Figure 8: Computational cost comparison of finetuning scGPT, scPEFT, Comparisons were performed under the batch correction protocol on the Perirhinal Cortex dataset using a system equipped with dual AMD EPYC 7643 (Milan, 2.3 GHz) processors  delivering  7-11  tera-floating-point  operations  per  second  (TFLOPS),  300  GB  of physical memory, and an NVIDIA A100 GPU with 40 GB memory and 19.5 TFLOPS of peak Supplementary Figure 9: Hyperparameter sensitivity analysis of scPEFT with scGPT as the backbone . a-b, Balanced accuracies for cell type identification on the COVID-19 and NSCLC datasets plotted against the number of learnable parameters for adapters with varying hidden representation  dimensions.  Larger  stars  represent  configurations  with  higher  intermediate embedding  dimensions,  which  correspond  to  more  tunable  parameters.  The  default  scPEFT setting is highlighted. c-f, Mean squared error at the top 20 differentially expressed genes (MSEDE)  for  perturbation  response  prediction  on  the  Adamson,  Norman,  Replogle\_k562,  and Replogle\_rpe1  datasets,  plotted  against  adapter  size. g-I, Overall  scores  for  batch  effect correction  on  the  PBMC-10k,  Perirhinal  Cortex,  and  COVID-19  datasets,  also  plotted  against learnable parameters under different adapter configurations.
