ncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"Introduces xVERSE as a transcriptomics-native foundation model for representation learning and virtual cell synthesis. The abstract explicitly contrasts it with language-model architectures, so no text component is supported here.","evidence_snippet":"\"a transcriptomics-native foundation model\" and \"Current single-cell foundation models rely on language-model architectures\""},{"record_id":"rec_000253","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The title indicates a gene set foundation model, but the record does not support a substantive text or language component. It is centered on biological gene sets rather than text-bio bridging.","evidence_snippet":"\"gene set foundation model pre-trained on a massive collection of diverse gene sets\""},{"record_id":"rec_000254","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"ChromFound is presented as a universal foundation model for single-cell chromatin accessibility data. The record supports a biological modality but not a text/language component.","evidence_snippet":"\"A Universal Foundation Model for Single-Cell Chromatin Accessibiltiy Data\""},{"record_id":"rec_000255","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"FLAG is a foundation model for spatial gene expression prediction, which is a biological modeling task. The abstract does not support any substantive text component.","evidence_snippet":"\"Foundation model representation ... for spatial