ask is to classify cell type, which is not generative. No generative mechanism mentioned.", "pilot_roundA_scope_gate": "UNCERTAIN", "pilot_roundA_architecture_gate": "UNCERTAIN", "pilot_needs_adjudication": true, "round-B_adjudicator_output": {"paper_type": "unclear", "bio_modality_present": "yes", "text_component_present": "unclear", "text_bio_bridge_present": "unclear", "generative_model_present": "no", "foundation_model_evidence": "unclear", "primary_exclusion_code": "EC3_not_generative", "uncertainty_reason": "none", "evidence_for_text_component": "none", "evidence_for_text_bio_bridge": "none", "evidence_for_generative_model": "classify the cell type", "boundary_case": "clear_exclude", "decision_rationale": "The abstract describes a cell-type classification task with no mention of generative mechanism (decoder, autoregressive, diffusion, etc.), so generative_model_present=no, leading to exclusion."}, "round-B_adjudicator_paper_type": "unclear", "round-B_adjudicator_bio_modality_present": "yes", "round-B_adjudicator_text_component_present": "unclear", "round-B_adjudicator_text_bio_bridge_present": "unclear", "round-B_adjudicator_generative_model_present": "no", "round-B_adjudicator_foundation_model_evidence": "unclear", "round-B_adjudicator_primary_exclusion_code": "EC3_not_generative", "round-B_adjudicator_uncertainty_reason": "none", "round-B_adjudicator_evidence_for_text_component": "none", "round-B_adjudicator_evidence_for_text_bio_bridge": "none", "round-B_adjudicator_evidence_for_generative_model": "classify the cell type", "round-B_adjudicator_boundary_case": "clear_exclude", "round-B_adjudicator_decision_rationale": "The abstract describes a cell-type classification task with no mention of generative mechanism (decoder, autoregressive, diffusion, etc.), so generative_model_present=no, leading to exclusion."}
./analysis/screening_run_artifacts_after_prompt_update_20260511/full_runs/deepseek_v4_review_pipeline_all4027_current_rep2_watchdog_20260510T013948Z/job_11505/guideline_pilot_results_partial.csv:75:1477,Harnessing the Power of Single-Cell Large Language Models with Parameter Efficient Fine-Tuning using scPEFT,harnessing the power of singlecell large language models with parameter efficient finetuning using scpeft,10.1038/s42256-025-01170-z,,40313770.0,,"He et al. present a parameter-efficient fine-tuning method for single-cell language models that improves performance on unseen diseases, treatments and cell types. Single-cell large language models (scLLMs) capture essential biological insights from vast single-cell atlases but struggle in out-of-context applications, where zero-shot predictions can be unreliable. To address this, here we introduce a single-cell parameter-efficient fine-tuning (scPEFT) framework that integrates learnable, low-dimensional adapters into scLLMs. By freezing the backbone model and updating only the adapter parameters, scPEFT efficiently adapts to specific tasks using limited custom data. This approach mitigates catastrophic forgetting, reduces parameter tuning by over 96% and decreases GPU memory usage by more than half, thus substantially enhancing the accessibility of scLLMs for resource-constrained researchers. When validated across diverse datasets, scPEFT outperformed zero-shot models and traditional fine-tuning in disease-specific, cross-species and undercharacterized cell population tasks. Its attention-mechanism analysis identified COVID-related genes associated with specific cell states and uncovered unique blood cell subpopulations, demonstrating the capacity of scPEFT for condition-specific interpretations. These findings position scPEFT as an efficient solution for enhancing the utility of scLLMs in general single-cell analyses.",Fei He; Ruixin Fei; Jordan E. Krull; Xinyu Zhang; Mingyue Gao; Li Su; Yibo Chen; Yang Yu; Jinpu Li; Baichuan Jin; Yuzhou Chang; A. Ma; Qin Ma; Dong Xu,2025.0,bioRxiv,2025-04-23,,"['google_scholar', 'semantic_scholar', 'springernature']",3,['10.1038/s42256-025-01170-z'],3,,,,,28,"{""paper_type"": ""unclear"", ""bio_modality_present"": ""yes"", ""text_component_present"": ""no"", ""text_bio_bridge_present"": ""no"", ""primary_exclusion_code"": ""EC2_no_text_component"", ""uncertainty_reason"": ""none"", ""evidence_for_text_component"": ""none"", ""evidence_for_text_bio_bridge"": ""none"", ""evidence_for_generative_model"": ""not_assessed"", ""boundary_case"": ""clear_exclude"", ""decision_rationale"": ""The abstract describes a fine-tuning method (scPEFT) for single-cell large language models, which are biological-token models, not natural-language text models. No text component or text-bio bridge is mentioned, so the record is excluded.""}",unclear,yes,no,no,EC2_no_text_component,none,none,none,not_assessed,clear_exclude,"The abstract describes a fine-tuning method (scPEFT) for single-cell large language models, which are biological-token models, not natural-language text models. No text component or text-bio bridge is mentioned, so the record is excluded.","{""paper_type"": ""application_wrapper"", ""generative_model_present"": ""no"", ""foundation_model_evidence"": ""no"", ""primary_exclusion_code"": ""application_wrapper"", ""uncertainty_reason"": ""none"", ""evidence_for_text_component"": ""not_assessed"", ""evidence_for_text_bio_bridge"": ""not_assessed"", ""evidence_for_generative_model"": ""none"", ""boundary_case"": ""wrapper_boundary"", ""decision_rationale"": ""The abstract describes scPEFT as a parameter-efficient fine-tuning method for existing single-cell large language models, not as a new generative architecture. The paper's contribution is a wrapper around pre-existing generative models, with no description of a generative mechanism for the candidate model.""}",application_wrapper,no,no,application_wrapper,none,not_assessed,not_assessed,none,wrap