./data/screening_codex_full_2026-07-06/role_logs/scope_reviewer/batch_0380.stderr.log:2028:data/screening_codex_full_2026-07-06/role_logs/scope_reviewer/batch_0208.response.txt:1:{"results":[{"record_id":"rec_001657","paper_type":"benchmark_resource","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"benchmark_resource","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"Abstract frames the work as benchmarking BCR sequencing technologies and explicitly says it generates a resource for the community. It is about immune repertoire sequencing, not a text-bio model.","evidence_snippet":"“benchmarking experiment” and “generated a resource for the immunology community”"},{"record_id":"rec_001658","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"unclear","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"text_bio_bridge_unclear","decision_rationale":"This is a Comment that discusses the landscape and barriers around single-cell large language models rather than presenting a new model. It mentions biomedical single-cell omics and LLMs, but not a specific primary text-bio bridge.","evidence_snippet":"“In this Comment, we examine the current landscape of scLLMs”"},{"record_id":"rec_001659","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"unclear","text_bio_bridge_present":"unclear","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"text_component_unclear","decision_rationale":"The abstract reads as a forward-looking commentary on virtual cells, organs, and foundation models rather than a primary model paper. It does not clearly specify a substantive text/language component.","evidence_snippet":"“Navigating the Deep Waters of Medical AI Models” and “Ultimately, the trajectory...”"},{"record_id":"rec_001660","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This presents a new generative self-expression model for single-cell and spatial multimodal data. The abstract describes omics integration and representation learning, but no substantive text/language component.","evidence_snippet":"“we propose a contrastive and generative deep self-expression model” for “single-cell and spatial multimodal data”"},{"record_id":"rec_001661","paper_type":"application_wrapper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The work reuses pre-trained DNA language models and compares embedding-based pipelines versus fine-tuning for downstream genomic prediction. That is an application of existing models, not a new substantive text-bio model.","evidence_snippet":"“Large pre-trained DNA language models” and “embedding-based pipelines”"},{"record_id":"rec_001662","paper_type":"application_wrapper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"FEDKEA integrates a pretrained protein language model with KNN for enzyme annotation, which is a downstream application pipeline around existing model embeddings. The abstract does not support a new text-bio foundation model with a substantive bridge.","evidence_snippet":"“integrates ESM-2 and distance-weighted KNN” for “enzyme function annotation”"},{"record_id":"rec_001663","paper_type":"unclear","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"paper_type_unclear","decision_rationale":"This is a genomic data compression/encoding paper, not a generative text-bio model paper. The abstract describes direct coding of DNA bases and does not mention any text or language component.","evidence_snippet":"“two-bit coding” for “genomic sequence” compression"},{"record_id":"rec_001664","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract explicitly says this review synthesizes the technology and applications of droplet-based scRNA-seq. It is a review, not a primary model paper.","evidence_snippet":"“This review synthesizes the technological evolution” of droplet-based single-cell RNA sequencing"}]}
