./data/docling_include_no_vlm_2026-07-09/chunks/full_2026_07_06_rec_001358.jsonl:77:{"candidate_id": "full_2026-07-06__rec_001358", "chunk_index": 77, "text": "\nCell type identification, Metrics = Balanced accuracy. Cell type identification, Brief description = The mean of true positive rates was computed for each cell type, ensuring equal weight across minority and majority classes.. Cell type identification, Metrics = Confusion matrix. Cell type identification, Brief description = A square matrix where rows denote actual cell types and columns denote predicted ones; diagonal entries indicate true positives per cell type, while off-diagonal entries capture misclassifications between cell types.. TF identification, Metrics = ROC-AUC. TF identification, Brief description = The area under the receiver operating characteristic curve (ROC-AUC) plots true positive rate against false positive rate across thresholds. Values near 1 reflect strong TF and non-TF separation, while 0.5 indicates random performance.. Cell group discovery, Metrics = CHI. Cell group discovery, Brief description = The Calinski-Harabasz index (CHI) quantifies cell group discovery as the ratio of between-group to within-cell group variance, with higher scores denoting more compact and well- separated cell groups.. Batch Correction, Metrics = NMI. Batch Correction, Brief description = The normalized mutual information (NMI) measures the agreement between cell-type", "contextualized_text": "Harnessing the power of single-cell large language models with parameter-efficient fine-tuning using scPEFT\nSupplementary Tables\nSupplementary Table 2: Evaluation metrics used in this study.\n\nCell type identification, Metrics = Balanced accuracy. Cell type identification, Brief description = The mean of true positive rates was computed for each cell type, ensuring equal weight across minority and majority classes.. Cell type identification, Metrics = Confusion matrix. Cell type identification, Brief description = A square matrix where rows denote actual cell types and columns denote predicted ones; diagonal entries indicate true positives per cell type, while off-diagonal entries capture misclassifications between cell types.. TF identification, Metrics = ROC-AUC. TF identification, Brief description = The area under the receiver operating characteristic curve (ROC-AUC) plots true positive rate against false positive rate across thresholds. Values near 1 reflect strong TF and non-TF separation, while 0.5 indicates random performance.. Cell group discovery, Metrics = CHI. Cell group discovery, Brief description = The Calinski-Harabasz index (CHI) quantifies cell group discovery as the ratio of between-group to within-cell group variance, with higher scores denoting more compact and well- separated cell groups.. Batch Correction, Metrics = NMI. Batch Correction, Brief description = The normalized mutual information (NMI) measures the agreement between cell-type", "headings": ["Harnessing the power of single-cell large language models with parameter-efficient fine-tuning using scPEFT", "Supplementary Tables", "Supplementary Table 2: Evaluation metrics used in this study."], "pages": [24], "meta": {"schema_name": "docling_core.transforms.chunker.DocMeta", "version": "1.0.0", "doc_items": [{"self_ref": "#/tables/1", "parent": {"cref": "#/body"}, "children": [], "content_layer": "body", "meta": null, "label": "table", "prov": [{"page_no": 24, "bbox": {"l": 70.19544219970703, "t": 680.4779510498047, "r": 540.4527587890625, "b": 73.7984619140625, "coord_origin": "BOTTOMLEFT"}, "charspan": [0, 0]}]}], "headings": ["Harnessing the power of single-cell large language models with parameter-efficient fine-tuning using scPEFT", "Supplementary Tables", "Supplementary Table 2: Evaluation metrics used in this study."], "captions": null, "origin": {"mimetype": "application/pdf", "binary_hash": 3578786038470275027, "filename": "full_text_02_landing_pdf_link.pdf", "uri": null}}}
./data/docling_include_no_vlm_2026-07-09/chunks/full_2026_07_06_rec_001358.jsonl:78:{"candidate_id": "full_2026-07-06__rec_001358", "chunk_index": 78, "text": "\n labels and Louvain clusters, normalized by their entropies (0 = no agreement, 1 = perfect match). Louvain clustering was performed across resolutions (0.1-2, step 0.1), with the clustering yielding the highest NMI reported.. Batch Correction, Metrics = ARI. Batch Correction, Brief description = The adjusted Rand index (ARI) considers both correct clustering overlaps while also counting correct disagreements between two clusters on the batch corrected data. The cell-type labels with the NMI-optimized Louvain clustering were used to compute ARI.. Batch Correction, Metrics = Cell-type ASW. Batch Correction, Brief description = The average silhouette width (ASW) score quantifies the match of each cell to its own cell type label relative to other clusters on the batch corrected data (scaled 0-1).. Batch Correction, Metrics = Avg BIO. Batch Correction, Brief description = Composite metric averaging NMI, ARI, and cell-type ASW to capture biological conservation.. Batch Correction, Metrics = Batch ASW. Batch Correction, Brief description = The average silhouette width is computed on batch labels, where 1 reflects ideal mixing and 0 indicates strong separation..", "contextualized_text": "Harnessing the power of single-cell large language models with parameter-efficient fine-tuning using scPEFT\nSupplementary Tables\nSupplementary Table 2: Evaluation metrics used in this study.\n\n labels and Louvain clusters, normalized by their entropies (0 = no agreement, 1 = perfect match). Louvain clustering was performed across resolutions (0.1-2, step 0.1), with the clustering yielding the highest NMI reported.. Batch Correction, Metrics = ARI. Batch Correction, Brief description = The adjusted Rand index (ARI) considers both correct clustering overlaps while also counting correct disagreements between two clusters on the batch corrected data. The cell-type labels with the NMI-optimized Louvain clustering were used to compute ARI.. Batch Correction, Metrics = Cell-type ASW. Batch Correction, Brief description = The average silhouette width (ASW) score quantifies the match of each cell to its own cell type label relative to other clusters on the batch corrected data (scaled 0-1).. Batch Correction, Metrics = Avg BIO. Batch Correction, Brief description = Composite metric averaging NMI, ARI, and cell-type ASW to capture biological conservation.. Batch Correction, Metrics = Batch ASW. Batch Correction, Brief description = The average silhouette width is computed on batch labels, where 1 reflects ideal mixing and 0 indicates strong separation..", "headings": ["Harnessing the power of single-cell large language models with parameter-efficient fine-tuning using scPEFT", "Supplementary Tables", "Supplementary Table 2: Evaluation metrics used in this study."], "pages": [24], "meta": {"schema_name": "docling_core.transforms.chunker.DocMeta", "version": "1.0.0", "doc_items": [{"self_ref": "#/tables/1", "parent": {"cref": "#/body"}, "children": [], "content_layer": "body", "meta": null, "label": "table", "prov": [{"page_no": 24, "bbox": {"l": 70.19544219970703, "t": 680.4779510498047, "r": 540.4527587890625, "b": 73.7984619140625, "coord_origin": "BOTTOMLEFT"}, "charspan": [0, 0]}]}], "headings": ["Harnessing the power of single-cell large language models with parameter-efficient fine-tuning using scPEFT", "Supplementary Tables", "Supplementary Table 2: Evaluation metrics used in this study."], "captions": null, "origin": {"mimetype": "application/pdf", "binary_hash": 3578786038470275027, "filename": "full_text_02_landing_pdf_link.pdf", "uri": null}}}
