./data/docling_include_no_vlm_2026-07-09/chunks/full_2026_07_06_rec_001358.jsonl:110:{"candidate_id": "full_2026-07-06__rec_001358", "chunk_index": 110, "text": "Supplementary Figure 4: UMAP visualizations of native, finetuned scLLMs, and scPEFT models with different backbones (a) scBERT, (b) Geneformer, (c) scFoundation and (d) scGPT, respectively, for cell type identification on the MS dataset.\nSupplementary Figure 5: UMAP visualizations of native, finetuned scLLMs, and scPEFT models with different backbones (a) scBERT, (b) Geneformer, (c) scFoundation and (d) scGPT, respectively, for cell type identification on the COVID dataset.\nSupplementary Figure 6: Confusion matrices for benchmarking cell type identification on the mouse, macaque, and C. elegans datasets. Confusion matrices illustrate the alignment between annotated and predicted cell types for native scGPT, finetuned scGPT, and scPEFT on the (a) mouse (b) macaque, and (c) C. elegans datasets.", "contextualized_text": "Harnessing the power of single-cell large language models with parameter-efficient fine-tuning using scPEFT\nSupplementary Figures\nSupplementary Figure 4: UMAP visualizations of native, finetuned scLLMs, and scPEFT models with different backbones (a) scBERT, (b) Geneformer, (c) scFoundation and (d) scGPT, respectively, for cell type identification on the MS dataset.\nSupplementary Figure 5: UMAP visualizations of native, finetuned scLLMs, and scPEFT models with different backbones (a) scBERT, (b) Geneformer, (c) scFoundation and (d) scGPT, respectively, for cell type identification on the COVID dataset.\nSupplementary Figure 6: Confusion matrices for benchmarking cell type identification on the mouse, macaque, and C. elegans datasets. Confusion matrices illustrate the alignment between annotated and predicted cell types for native scGPT, finetuned scGPT, and scPEFT on the (a) mouse (b) macaque, and (c) C. elegans datasets.", "headings": ["Harnessing the power of single-cell large language models with parameter-efficient fine-tuning using scPEFT", "Supplementary Figures"], "pages": [34, 35, 36], "meta": {"schema_name": "docling_core.transforms.chunker.DocMeta", "version": "1.0.0", "doc_items": [{"self_ref": "#/texts/195", "parent": {"cref": "#/pictures/3"}, "children": [], "content_layer": "body", "meta": null, "label": "caption", "prov": [{"page_no": 34, "bbox": {"l": 72.0, "t": 172.78463999999997, "r": 543.1827840000017, "b": 133.74830532596684, "coord_origin": "BOTTOMLEFT"}, "charspan": [0, 237]}]}, {"self_ref": "#/texts/197", "parent": {"cref": "#/pictures/4"}, "children": [], "content_layer": "body", "meta": null, "label": "caption", "prov": [{"page_no": 35, "bbox": {"l": 72.0, "t": 167.50463999999988, "r": 543.1827840000017, "b": 128.70830532596688, "coord_origin": "BOTTOMLEFT"}, "charspan": [0, 240]}]}, {"self_ref": "#/texts/199", "parent": {"cref": "#/pictures/5"}, "children": [], "content_layer": "body", "meta": null, "label": "caption", "prov": [{"page_no": 36, "bbox": {"l": 72.0, "t": 155.02463999999998, "r": 543.183312, "b": 101.82830532596677, "coord_origin": "BOTTOMLEFT"}, "charspan": [0, 324]}]}], "headings": ["Harnessing the power of single-cell large language models with parameter-efficient fine-tuning using scPEFT", "Supplementary Figures"], "captions": null, "origin": {"mimetype": "application/pdf", "binary_hash": 3578786038470275027, "filename": "full_text_02_landing_pdf_link.pdf", "uri": null}}}
