./data/docling_include_no_vlm_2026-07-09/chunks/full_2026_07_06_rec_001358.jsonl:119:{"candidate_id": "full_2026-07-06__rec_001358", "chunk_index": 119, "text": "Supplementary Figure 21: Comparison of cell embeddings from native, finetuned scGPT, and scPEFT adapted to a lung cancer atlas. a, UMAP visualizations of all cell embeddings generated  by  native  scGPT,  finetuned  scGPT,  and  scPEFT,  colored  by  major  cell  type annotations from the lung cancer atlas. b, UMAP visualizations of epithelial cell embeddings from each model, colored by fine-grained cell type annotations. c, UMAP visualizations of cancer cell embeddings, colored by their UICC stage annotations. d-e, Bar plots of CHI scores for each model, comparing ( d ) all cell embeddings across major cell types and epithelial cell embeddings across fine cell type categories.", "contextualized_text": "Harnessing the power of single-cell large language models with parameter-efficient fine-tuning using scPEFT\nSupplementary Figures\nSupplementary Figure 21: Comparison of cell embeddings from native, finetuned scGPT, and scPEFT adapted to a lung cancer atlas. a, UMAP visualizations of all cell embeddings generated  by  native  scGPT,  finetuned  scGPT,  and  scPEFT,  colored  by  major  cell  type annotations from the lung cancer atlas. b, UMAP visualizations of epithelial cell embeddings from each model, colored by fine-grained cell type annotations. c, UMAP visualizations of cancer cell embeddings, colored by their UICC stage annotations. d-e, Bar plots of CHI scores for each model, comparing ( d ) all cell embeddings across major cell types and epithelial cell embeddings across fine cell type categories.", "headings": ["Harnessing the power of single-cell large language models with parameter-efficient fine-tuning using scPEFT", "Supplementary Figures"], "pages": [51], "meta": {"schema_name": "docling_core.transforms.chunker.DocMeta", "version": "1.0.0", "doc_items": [{"self_ref": "#/texts/229", "parent": 